<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Necho I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 664 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Necho I was a ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sais">Sais</a> in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a> in the 7th century BCE and the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/psamtik-i">Psamtik I</a>, founder of the Twenty-sixth Dynasty. He became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esarhaddon">Esarhaddon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashurbanipal">Ashurbanipal</a> drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushites</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and was briefly taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> before being restored. He was killed in 664 BCE when the Kushite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tantamani">Tantamani</a> invaded Egypt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/necho-i.jpg" alt="Necho I" width="267" height="433" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flinders Petrie (1853-1942) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Necho_I_Horus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
